# Push every change to GitHub

This app is used via **GitHub Pages** (`https://sonatudu.github.io/ba/`). Local-only builds are not enough.

After finishing user-requested code changes:

1. Run `npm run build` when frontend files changed.
2. Also run `npm run build:android` (`vite build` + `cap sync android`) so Android Studio’s copy in `android/app/src/main/assets` matches. GitHub Pages is **not** what Android Studio runs.
3. Commit the relevant source changes (not `android/.idea/`, secrets, or unrelated junk).
4. `git push origin HEAD` (or the current feature branch) so Pages/Actions can deploy.
5. Tell the user: the website updates after deploy; for Android Studio they only need to press **Run** (green play) on the phone. Do not tell them to hard-refresh the website.

Do this continuously for Ba work unless the user explicitly says not to push.
